# WP-238 Part 4's cxx-comdat-last-use pair (live_pairs.rs): `twice` is a
# COMDAT in a.o (elected; its user fa dead) and in b.o; main.o's call of
# fb is its last live use. EDIT removes it: fb's and twice's sections die.
proves: a COMDAT function's last live use removed under --gc-sections is judged by live::live against the front's mark, and the update falls back (layout) by name while the placement flips
source: WP-238 Part 4 ("Step 2 Part 4", cxx-comdat-last-use); WP-225 gc-lift; back in the lane with the dry run's .eh_frame hole (WP-225 M2b-2d gc-3)
edit: main.cc
link: main.o a.o b.o
cflags: -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections
options: --gc-sections
expect-full: update-not-implemented (layout|symtab|scan): a section that dies or revives changes the stored placement (SECTIONS.bits, META.live_hash), which the image takes only from M2b-3 on (WP-225 gc-lift), and the placement refuses an unchanged file the live delta draws in, whose layout inputs are not produced (WP-225 M2b-2d) WP-225 M2b-4: a drawn-in file's layout inputs are produced (fresh ids), and the hop then falls back by a later producer's name: the materializer's `(symtab)` (a drawn-in file's local span or `.symtab` size changes: no symtab plan is wired), the scan's `(scan)` (F-1: a key the drawn-in file defines has a new RESOLVED row, its section the fresh id), or `layout_in`'s `(layout)` (a merge section marked in part).
compilers: gcc kiln
